      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. you called it a \"fundamental requirement\" rather than just a choice. can you go deeper into the security side of that? specifically, why is a \"Zero-Latency\" model—incorporating things like real-time biometric and facial recognition—considered the only way to stay ahead of modern threats, compared to just increasing the number of officers or using upgraded manual surveillance? i need to justify why the old ways are basically dead end solutions.",
