      "content": "i see. one big hurdle we're going to hit with the board is the inevitable backlash from privacy groups and civil liberties advocates. they're going to argue that this level of biometric surveillance is a massive overreach and a violation of fundamental rights.\n\nhow should we address those specific pushbacks in our roadmap? i'm looking for ways to frame the necessity of these systems so that the privacy objections don't end up stalling the implementation.",
